(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF TEXTILES) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: AMENDED TECHNOLOGY UPGRADATION FUND SCHEME \(ATUFS\) \(ATUFS\) / OFFICE OF TEXTILE COMMISSIONER / MINISTRY OF TEXTILES) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Capital investment subsidy for the modernization and technology induction) Tj
T*
(in textile segments including garmenting, technical textiles, weaving, and) Tj
T*
(processing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Entity engaged in textile manufacturing intending to install benchmarked) Tj
T*
(   state-of-the-art machinery.) Tj
T*
(2. Must obtain Unique Identification Number \(UID\) from i-TUFS portal prior) Tj
T*
(   to machinery acquisition.) Tj
T*
(3. Term loan availed from notified lending banks/financial institutions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Capital Investment Subsidy \(CIS\) of 10% to 15% on eligible benchmarked) Tj
T*
(   machinery with a subsidy ceiling up to Rs. 30 Crore depending on textile) Tj
T*
(   sub-segment.) Tj
T*
(2. Concession or margin money subsidy rate of 15.0 % subsidy.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 30.00 Crore per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. i-TUFS UID certificate) Tj
T*
(2. Bank sanction letter and appraisal note) Tj
T*
(3. Commercial invoices and customs clearance for imported textile machines) Tj
T*
(4. Chartered Engineer commissioning certificate) Tj
T*
(5. Factory registration and pollution NOC) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via i-TUFS Portal) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://itufs.gov.in/) Tj
T*
